<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sharaf Khan Bidlisi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1543–c. 1603</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sharaf Khan Bidlisi was a Kurdish emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bitlis">Bitlis</a> and historian, born in 1543 and raised at the Safavid court. After serving the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavids</a> he went over to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>, who restored him as ruler of his family's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> of Bitlis in 1578. In 1597 he completed in Persian the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sharafnama">Sharafnama</a>, a history of the Kurdish dynasties and the first major work of Kurdish history.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sharaf-khan-bidlisi.jpg" alt="Sharaf Khan Bidlisi" width="320" height="407" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 1582, Nusretname · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sharaf_khan_(portrait)_exchanging_the_Safavid_turban_for_the_Ottoman_headdress.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
